@startuml
skinparam {
    ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BoundaryBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ControlBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    EntityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

    ActorBorderColor black
    BoundaryBorderColor black
    ControlBorderColor black
    EntityBorderColor black
    DatabaseBorderColor black
}

actor User
boundary "Reply Section (UI)" as UI
boundary Router
control ReplyController
control ReplyService
entity VoteReplyModel
database MongoDB

User -> UI: 1. Click Reply Downvote
activate User
activate UI

UI -> Router: 2. POST /downvote (reply)
activate Router

Router -> ReplyController: 3. downVote(reply_id, req)
activate ReplyController

opt Token / Role Invalid
    ReplyController --> Router: 3.1.1 401 / 403 Error
    Router --> UI: 3.1.2 Show error
    UI --> User: 3.1.3 Error message
end

ReplyController -> ReplyService: 4. downVote(reply_id, payload)
activate ReplyService

ReplyService -> ReplyService: 5. checkLegitUser(payload)
activate ReplyService

alt User not valid
    ReplyService --> ReplyController: 5.1.1 Error
    deactivate ReplyService
    ReplyController --> Router: 5.1.2 Error response
    Router --> UI: 5.1.3 Show error
    UI --> User: 5.1.4 Error message
else User is banned
    ReplyService --> ReplyController: 5.2.1 Error
    ReplyController --> Router: 5.2.2 Error response
    Router --> UI: 5.2.3 Show error
    UI --> User: 5.2.4 Error message
end

ReplyService -> VoteReplyModel: 6. findOne(reply_id, user_id)
activate VoteReplyModel
VoteReplyModel -> MongoDB: 7. query vote
activate MongoDB
MongoDB --> VoteReplyModel: 8. existingVote / null
deactivate MongoDB
VoteReplyModel --> ReplyService: 9. result
deactivate VoteReplyModel

alt No existing vote
    ReplyService -> VoteReplyModel: 9.1.1 create new vote (is_up=false)
    activate VoteReplyModel
    VoteReplyModel -> MongoDB: 9.1.2 insert vote
    activate MongoDB
    MongoDB --> VoteReplyModel: 9.1.3 inserted document
    deactivate MongoDB
    VoteReplyModel --> ReplyService: 9.1.4 created vote
    deactivate VoteReplyModel
    ReplyService --> ReplyController: 9.1.5 Reply downvoted
    ReplyController --> Router: 9.1.6 Reply downvoted response
    Router --> UI: 9.1.7 Update reply vote state
    UI --> User: 9.1.8 See updated reply downvote
else Existing vote is down
    ReplyService -> VoteReplyModel: 9.2.1 delete vote
    activate VoteReplyModel
    VoteReplyModel -> MongoDB: 9.2.2 delete document
    activate MongoDB
    MongoDB --> VoteReplyModel: 9.2.3 deletion confirmation
    deactivate MongoDB
    VoteReplyModel --> ReplyService: 9.2.4 vote deleted
    deactivate VoteReplyModel
    ReplyService --> ReplyController: 9.2.5 Reply downvote removed
    ReplyController --> Router: 9.2.6 Reply downvote removed response
    Router --> UI: 9.2.7 Update reply vote state
    UI --> User: 9.2.8 See removed reply downvote
else Existing vote is up
    ReplyService -> VoteReplyModel: 9.3.1 update is_up=false
    activate VoteReplyModel
    VoteReplyModel -> MongoDB: 9.3.2 update document
    activate MongoDB
    MongoDB --> VoteReplyModel: 9.3.3 updated document
    deactivate MongoDB
    VoteReplyModel --> ReplyService: 9.3.4 vote updated
    deactivate VoteReplyModel
    ReplyService --> ReplyController: 9.3.5 Reply downvoted
    deactivate ReplyService
    ReplyController --> Router: 9.3.6 Reply downvoted response
    deactivate ReplyController
    Router --> UI: 9.3.7 Update reply vote state
    deactivate Router
    UI --> User: 9.3.8 See updated reply downvote
    deactivate UI
    deactivate User
end
@enduml
